From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] egl: sRGB window configs on surfaceless with kopper

Surfaceless with kopper (0024) adds its window configs from the pbuffer
visuals, which list linear formats only, so the driver's sRGB configs
never joined an EGL config: eglCreateWindowSurface with
EGL_GL_COLORSPACE_SRGB failed with EGL_BAD_MATCH, and a WGL window with
an sRGB-capable pixel format (WGL_FRAMEBUFFER_SRGB_CAPABLE_ARB) had no
surface on iOS. A window config's sRGB variant now joins its linear
visual's EGL config, as on Wayland; pbuffer-only configs are unchanged.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-opengl-wgl-completeness.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
index 495c37f..893d8a8 100644
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
@@ -503,7 +503,12 @@ dri2_add_pbuffer_configs_for_visuals(_EGLDisplay *disp, EGLint surface_type)
       EGLint config_group = 0;
       struct gl_config *gl_config =
          (struct gl_config *) dri2_dpy->driver_configs[i];
-      int idx = dri2_pbuffer_visual_index(gl_config->color_format);
+      enum pipe_format format = gl_config->color_format;
+      /* A window config's sRGB variant joins its linear visual's EGL config,
+       * as on Wayland, so EGL_GL_COLORSPACE_SRGB finds it. */
+      if (surface_type & EGL_WINDOW_BIT)
+         format = util_format_linear(format);
+      int idx = dri2_pbuffer_visual_index(format);
 
       if (idx == -1)
          continue;
